TITLE:: MapperWindow
summary:: the mapper's window: controllers, targets, learn, every mapping
categories:: Libraries>Mapper
related:: Classes/Mapper, Classes/MapperMap

DESCRIPTION::
code::
Mapper.default.gui;
Mapper.default.gui.select([\tidal, \cut]);
::

On the left, everything that can be mapped now, provider by provider and group by group,
narrowed by the menu and by what is typed in the field; a star marks the mapped ones. Pick a row
and it is on show on the right.

On the right, the controllers: strong::find:: lists the devices plugged in, strong::connect::
listens to one under a name, strong::forget:: lets it go with its mappings. Then the mappings,
by controller and element, so the targets of one control sit together - the second and later
ones start with a plus. Under the list, the one on show: lo and hi in the target's own units,
invert, takeover, the button mode and the curve, which is drawn by dragging its points.

strong::midi learn:: switches the mapper's learn mode: click a fader, a knob or a switch in any
window that follows it, move a control, and again until it is off. strong::learn:: maps the next
element moved to the target on show; a control that already moves something keeps that as well.
strong::+ tidal:: learns a Tidal control by name, strong::code...:: opens every mapping as code.

The window keeps nothing: closing it changes no mapping.

